286
00:12:40,080 --> 00:12:41,380
You're a man on a mission.

287
00:12:41,740 --> 00:12:42,080
Mm-hmm.

288
00:12:42,360 --> 00:12:43,520
Everybody has something

289
00:12:43,520 --> 00:12:44,860
that's missing from their lives,

290
00:12:44,920 --> 00:12:45,480
even me.

291
00:12:45,840 --> 00:12:47,440
If I can fill that void...

292
00:12:47,440 --> 00:12:49,880
Crap.

293
00:12:50,380 --> 00:12:51,780
We just fed him his own line.

294
00:12:54,780 --> 00:12:56,540
You and I have a lot in common.

295
00:12:56,840 --> 00:12:59,100
That happens to be my philosophy in life.

296
00:12:59,820 --> 00:13:01,560
When I teach a sixth grade class,

297
00:13:01,560 --> 00:13:03,920
I like to bring it up in my graduation speech.

298
00:13:04,800 --> 00:13:06,880
It sort of ties into what you said

299
00:13:06,880 --> 00:13:08,640
